content.thinking:
Now IdempotencyService. It wraps business in a TransactionTemplate so request_log insert and business commit atomically. But TranslationService methods are @Transactional — when called from IdempotencyService's TransactionTemplate, they join (REQUIRED default). Good.

But careful: IdempotencyService.execute calls business supplier which calls translationService methods (proxied, @Transactional joins existing tx). Good.

IdempotencyService:

```java
@Service
public class IdempotencyService {
    public record StoredResponse(int status, String body) {}
    public record Fingerprint(String method, String path, String actor, Object payload) {}

    execute(String requestId, Fingerprint fp, Supplier<Object> business):
        if blank requestId -> badRequest
        String hash = sha256(json(fp))
        var existing = requestLogs.find(requestId)
        if present: hash match ? stored : throw requestConflict
        try {
            return txTemplate.execute(tx -> {
                Object result = business.get();
                String body = objectMapper.writeValueAsString(result);
                requestLogs.insert(requestId, hash, 200, body, Instant.now(clock));
                return new StoredResponse(200, body);
            });
        } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
            var row = requestLogs.find(requestId).orElseThrow(() -> e);
            if (row.requestHash().equals(hash)) return new StoredResponse(row.status(), row.response());
            throw ApiException.requestConflict(...);
        }
}
```

Note: serialization exception inside tx — wrap in unchecked. ObjectMapper writeValueAsString throws JsonProcessingException (checked) — wrap in UncheckedIOException or IllegalStateException.

SHA-256: MessageDigest.

Also note: business exceptions (ApiException) propagate out of txTemplate.execute → rollback → no request_log. Good — 失败不占键.

One subtlety: requestLog find before tx uses auto-commit read; fine.

